Summary: Roll out two-factor authentication across retail digital banking application

Business Case
Retail login is single-factor today. Q2 saw 214 credential-stuffing-linked unauthorised access attempts, with ₹1.4 Cr in disputed transactions and an average of 46 contact-centre minutes per fraud case. The current flow also does not satisfy RBI's additional-factor requirement on digital channels, which is an open finding from the March internal audit with a remediation deadline. Three enterprise-adjacent partnerships have flagged it as a gate.

Expected outcome: eliminate the audit finding, reduce account-takeover cases by ≥80%, and close the partnership blocker.

Goals

Meet the RBI additional-factor requirement on internet and mobile banking before the audit deadline
Introduce a second factor at login and at high-risk transaction checkpoints without materially increasing drop-off
Give Fraud Ops and Contact Centre the tooling and runbooks to support customers through it